Clerk: Yes, you can pay half now and half before the third week. But registration closes this Thursday, so please don''t wait too long.
Student: That''s fine. Do I need to bring anything?
Clerk: A copy of your ID and one passport-size photo. You can email the ID copy if you prefer.
Student: Great. I''ll come back tomorrow with the photo and pay the first half then.
Clerk: Perfect. See you tomorrow.', 'When does registration close?', '[{"id":"a","text":"Tomorrow"},{"id":"b","text":"This Thursday"},{"id":"c","text":"Next month"},{"id":"d","text":"Before the third week"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'The clerk warns that registration closes this Thursday.', 'easy', array['listening-comprehension','step-mock-2']::text[]) on conflict (id) do update set section = excluded.section, course_id = excluded.course_id, passage_id = excluded.passage_id, audio_url = excluded.audio_url, transcript = excluded.transcript, prompt = excluded.prompt, options = excluded.options, correct_option_id = excluded.correct_option_id, explanation = excluded.explanation, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, tags = excluded.tags;
insert into public.questions (id, section, course_id, passage_id, audio_url, transcript, prompt, options, correct_option_id, explanation, difficulty, tags) values ('sm2-listening-3', 'listening', null, null, null, 'Clerk: Good morning. How can I help you?
Student: Hi. I''d like to register for the evening English course that starts next month.
Clerk: Of course. The course meets on Sundays and Tuesdays from six to eight. The registration fee is four hundred and fifty riyals.
Student: Is it possible to pay in two parts?
Clerk: Yes, you can pay half now and half before the third week. But registration closes this Thursday, so please don''t wait too long.
Student: That''s fine. Do I need to bring anything?
Clerk: A copy of your ID and one passport-size photo. You can email the ID copy if you prefer.
Student: Great. I''ll come back tomorrow with the photo and pay the first half then.
Clerk: Perfect. See you tomorrow.', 'What will the student probably do tomorrow?', '[{"id":"a","text":"Email a copy of his ID only"},{"id":"b","text":"Pay the full fee online"},{"id":"c","text":"Bring a photo and pay half of the fee"},{"id":"d","text":"Attend the first class"}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'He says he will return tomorrow with the photo and pay the first half.', 'medium', array['listening-comprehension','listening-inference','step-mock-2']::text[]) on conflict (id) do update set section = excluded.section, course_id = excluded.course_id, passage_id = excluded.passage_id, audio_url = excluded.audio_url, transcript = excluded.transcript, prompt = excluded.prompt, options = excluded.options, correct_option_id = excluded.correct_option_id, explanation = excluded.explanation, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, tags = excluded.tags;
insert into public.questions (id, section, course_id, passage_id, audio_url, transcript, prompt, options, correct_option_id, explanation, difficulty, tags) values ('sm2-listening-4', 'listening', null, null, null, 'Lecturer: Today we will look at how volcanoes form. A volcano is an opening in the Earth''s crust through which hot melted rock, called magma, escapes to the surface. Most volcanoes are found where two of the Earth''s plates meet. The best-known example is the so-called Ring of Fire around the Pacific Ocean, which contains about three quarters of the world''s active volcanoes.
Student: Does that mean volcanoes are always dangerous?
Lecturer: Not necessarily. Some erupt gently, and the lava simply flows down the slopes. The dangerous ones are those where gas is trapped inside the magma, because the pressure builds until the volcano explodes. Interestingly, volcanic soil is very rich, which is why many farmers choose to live near them despite the risk.', 'What is the main topic of the lecture?', '[{"id":"a","text":"The history of the Pacific Ocean"},{"id":"b","text":"How farmers choose their land"},{"id":"c","text":"How to predict eruptions"},{"id":"d","text":"How and where volcanoes form"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'The lecturer opens with how volcanoes form and where they are found.', 'easy', array['listening-comprehension','step-mock-2']::text[]) on conflict (id) do update set section = excluded.section, course_id = excluded.course_id, passage_id = excluded.passage_id, audio_url = excluded.audio_url, transcript = excluded.transcript, prompt = excluded.prompt, options = excluded.options, correct_option_id = excluded.correct_option_id, explanation = excluded.explanation, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, tags = excluded.tags;
