Student: Does that mean volcanoes are always dangerous?
Lecturer: Not necessarily. Some erupt gently, and the lava simply flows down the slopes. The dangerous ones are those where gas is trapped inside the magma, because the pressure builds until the volcano explodes. Interestingly, volcanic soil is very rich, which is why many farmers choose to live near them despite the risk.', 'What makes some volcanoes explode?', '[{"id":"a","text":"Heavy rain on the slopes"},{"id":"b","text":"Trapped gas that raises the pressure"},{"id":"c","text":"Very cold lava"},{"id":"d","text":"Fast-moving plates"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'Dangerous volcanoes trap gas in the magma, and the pressure builds until they explode.', 'medium', array['listening-comprehension','step-mock-2']::text[]) on conflict (id) do update set section = excluded.section, course_id = excluded.course_id, passage_id = excluded.passage_id, audio_url = excluded.audio_url, transcript = excluded.transcript, prompt = excluded.prompt, options = excluded.options, correct_option_id = excluded.correct_option_id, explanation = excluded.explanation, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, tags = excluded.tags;
insert into public.questions (id, section, course_id, passage_id, audio_url, transcript, prompt, options, correct_option_id, explanation, difficulty, tags) values ('sm2-listening-6', 'listening', null, null, null, 'Lecturer: Today we will look at how volcanoes form. A volcano is an opening in the Earth''s crust through which hot melted rock, called magma, escapes to the surface. Most volcanoes are found where two of the Earth''s plates meet. The best-known example is the so-called Ring of Fire around the Pacific Ocean, which contains about three quarters of the world''s active volcanoes.
Student: Does that mean volcanoes are always dangerous?
Lecturer: Not necessarily. Some erupt gently, and the lava simply flows down the slopes. The dangerous ones are those where gas is trapped inside the magma, because the pressure builds until the volcano explodes. Interestingly, volcanic soil is very rich, which is why many farmers choose to live near them despite the risk.', 'Why do some farmers live near volcanoes?', '[{"id":"a","text":"Eruptions are easy to predict."},{"id":"b","text":"The land is cheap."},{"id":"c","text":"The soil is very rich."},{"id":"d","text":"The air is cleaner."}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'The lecturer says volcanic soil is very rich, which is why farmers live nearby despite the risk.', 'medium', array['listening-comprehension','listening-inference','step-mock-2']::text[]) on conflict (id) do update set section = excluded.section, course_id = excluded.course_id, passage_id = excluded.passage_id, audio_url = excluded.audio_url, transcript = excluded.transcript, prompt = excluded.prompt, options = excluded.options, correct_option_id = excluded.correct_option_id, explanation = excluded.explanation, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, tags = excluded.tags;
insert into public.questions (id, section, course_id, passage_id, audio_url, transcript, prompt, options, correct_option_id, explanation, difficulty, tags) values ('sm2-listening-7', 'listening', null, null, null, 'Receptionist: Dr. Hassan''s clinic, how can I help?
Caller: Hello, this is Khalid Omar. I have an appointment on Monday at ten, but I''m afraid I have to change it. My brother is getting married and I''ll be travelling.
Receptionist: I see. Congratulations! Would Wednesday at half past four work?
Caller: Wednesday is fine, but I finish work at four and the clinic is far from my office. Could we make it five o''clock?
Receptionist: Let me check... yes, five o''clock is free on Wednesday.
Caller: Perfect. Thank you.
Receptionist: I''ll send you a text message to confirm.', 'Why does the caller want to change his appointment?', '[{"id":"a","text":"He is feeling much better."},{"id":"b","text":"He has a meeting at work."},{"id":"c","text":"The clinic is closed on Monday."},{"id":"d","text":"He will travel for his brother''s wedding."}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'He says his brother is getting married and he will be travelling.', 'easy', array['listening-comprehension','step-mock-2']::text[]) on conflict (id) do update set section = excluded.section, course_id = excluded.course_id, passage_id = excluded.passage_id, audio_url = excluded.audio_url, transcript = excluded.transcript, prompt = excluded.prompt, options = excluded.options, correct_option_id = excluded.correct_option_id, explanation = excluded.explanation, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, tags = excluded.tags;
